9.8 Checkpoint
Refer to the bottom two steps of workspace/_targets.R. We have fitted a mixed-effect meta-analysis model and written the results to a CSV file: outputs/health-wellbeing/meta-summary.csv.

read.csv(file.path(
  "outputs", "health-wellbeing", "meta-summary.csv"
)) |&gt; 
  dplyr::select(c("data_version", "data_scope", "data_filter", "pooled_r", "confidence_level", "tau2", "effect_scale", "tau_method", "meta_version")) |&gt;
  dplyr::mutate(across(where(is.numeric), ~ round(.x, 3))) |&gt; 
  tidyr::pivot_longer(
      cols = everything(),
      names_to = "metric",
      values_to = "value",
      values_transform = list(value = as.character)
    ) 

